# SDK first, hosts in parallel

Wire, classification, SOS lifecycle, and geo gates live in `eixam-sdk-flutter`. Host apps stay thin: typed SDK state in, public APIs out. No BLE byte decode, no duplicate `sosType` rules, no local 0°,0° accept list.

When a firmware/SDK contract changes, patch **eixam-app and eixam-sdk-demo-flutter in the same turn**. Same semantics both hosts: 7 B `sosType = 3` is open SOS, last-known pin keeps its age, Null Island is never painted, `ACK_SOS`/`0xE3` is not a user cancel.

Do not ship an app-only workaround that the demo still violates, or the reverse.
